# pushtest.gfrapp.com — iPhone Push Test preparation, isolated sandbox
# origin (Option B from Part 1's design).
#
# TEMPLATE ONLY. This file is NOT applied to any running Caddy instance and
# is not referenced by Caddyfile.production. It must not be copied in, and
# DNS for pushtest.gfrapp.com must not be created, until both are
# explicitly authorized in a future, separate part. When that happens, this
# block is additive: paste it in ALONGSIDE the existing app.gfrapp.com site
# block in ops/windows/caddy/Caddyfile.production (or a separately included
# file) -- it must never replace, merge into, or otherwise modify that
# block. The production app, API, and database are untouched by this file
# existing on disk; nothing reads it today.
#
# Topology this describes, once (and only once) applied:
#
#   Internet ──443──> Caddy, same instance already serving app.gfrapp.com
#                        │
#                        ├─ /submit ──> pushtest-receiver (127.0.0.1:8099,
#                        │               loopback only, same-origin so no
#                        │               CORS or mixed-content handling is
#                        │               needed)
#                        └─ /*       ──> static files under pushtest/web,
#                                        served directly, no build step
#
# Prerequisites before this template is ever copied in for real:
#   - A DNS A/AAAA record for pushtest.gfrapp.com, pointed at this same
#     host (Cloudflare, per the existing convention) -- not created by this
#     part.
#   - cmd/pushtest-receiver running locally (see pushtest/README.md),
#     started with its own GFR_PUSHTEST_RECEIVER_TOKEN.
#   - pushtest/web/config.js created locally from config.example.js, with
#     a real dev-only VAPID public key -- the receiver token is no longer
#     stored in any file (Part 2B correction): it is typed by hand into
#     the page itself at test time, never committed, never served.
#
# {$GFR_PUSHTEST_FRONTEND_ROOT} setup (corrected in Part 2B -- this was
# previously an undefined placeholder with no instructions at all):
# Caddy only ever sees an env var if the process that starts/reloads it
# has that var set first -- exactly how ops/windows/caddy/Run-Caddy.ps1
# sets $env:GFR_FRONTEND_ROOT (Run-Caddy.ps1:20) immediately before
# launching caddy.exe as its child process. This template does not modify
# Run-Caddy.ps1 (a production runtime script, out of scope for this
# preparation) and ships no code to set this variable permanently. When
# this template is actually applied, whoever does so must, in the exact
# same PowerShell session, before running `caddy run`/`caddy reload`:
#
#   $env:GFR_PUSHTEST_FRONTEND_ROOT = "<absolute path to pushtest/web>"
#
# If this ever becomes a longer-lived addition rather than a one-time
# test, the durable fix is one line in Run-Caddy.ps1 mirroring its own
# existing GFR_FRONTEND_ROOT line -- a separate, explicitly authorized
# change, not part of this template.

pushtest.gfrapp.com {
	encode gzip

	handle /submit {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8099
	}

	handle {
		root * {$GFR_PUSHTEST_FRONTEND_ROOT}
		file_server
	}

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		X-Frame-Options "DENY"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
	}
}
